Z||000012||2M4 Dale||03-21-2001||12:25 AM||||I figured it would be fun finding out what these are...lol. They were in an auto repair garage. With a bunch of 40's-50's parts sitting around in boxes......It's not a plane, although, it is from the Jet age. Auto manufacturors and artists really liked to emulate jets and planes into thier designs after the war and into the 50's. Tail fins...etc. I'm gonna keep diggin'...Thanks Guys for lookin'<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 03-21-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000013||Wolfhound||03-21-2001||06:05 AM||||2M4 Dale, Good post, It was raining and cold here yesterday and I searched about an hour for the answer. Ran across a lot of neat stuff but couldn't find it.<BR>They probably were inside the doors, being there is a right and left emblem. Yeah mid 40,s to early 50,s.<BR>Is anything embossed on the back? (numbers etc.)  ||||reg||1
